{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Now.</b> Since they had conquered the land of Sihon and Og." "<b>Will lick up the assembly all around us.</b> To expand their territory and secure it." "<b>Balak son of Zippor.</b> He was renowned as a mighty man of war." "<b>King of Moab at that time.</b> In any case, he did not summon the courage to wage war against Israel, as it says (Judges 11:25): הֲרֹב רָב עַם יִשְׂרָאֵל, אִם נִלְחוֹם נִלְחָם בָּם. And what Joshua says (Joshua 24:9), ״וַיָּקָם בָּלָק בֶּן צִפּוֹר מֶלֶךְ מוֹאָב וַיִּלָּחֶם בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל״ — he said this because he hired Balaam to curse them, as he explains by saying, ״וַיִּשְׁלַח וַיִּקְרָא לְבִלְעָם״."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:39.992932514Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}